                "title": "Deep mental model",
                "content": "For **Keywords**, build your understanding around three questions: what problem does the feature solve, what rules govern its behavior, and what assumptions must be true for it to be safe? This prevents memorization without understanding.\n\nStart with a minimal example, then vary one condition at a time. Pay particular attention to boundaries, invalid input, lifetime, type conversions, and failure paths. C gives the programmer considerable control, but that control also means the program often will not stop you from making an unsafe assumption.\n\nFor interviews, be able to explain the feature in plain language, write a small example without copying, identify one subtle edge case, and compare it with the closest alternative. That combination shows practical understanding."
