                "title": "Deep mental model",
                "content": "For **Function prototype**, think of a function as a contract between caller and callee. The contract includes parameter types, the return type, permitted inputs, side effects, and any ownership or lifetime assumptions. A function becomes easier to test when those assumptions are visible.\n\nC passes ordinary arguments by value. If a function must change caller-owned data, it normally receives an appropriate pointer. That distinction prevents the common mistake of expecting an ordinary parameter assignment to modify the caller's variable.\n\nGood decomposition separates calculation from I/O and keeps each function's responsibility narrow enough to describe clearly. For recursive functions, identify the base case and prove that each recursive step moves toward it. For library-facing code, also define what happens when input is invalid or an operation fails."
