                "title": "Deep mental model",
                "content": "The mental model for **Symbolic constants** is that a type is part of the program's contract. It affects representation, conversions, valid operations, function calls, and sometimes the range of values that can be represented.\n\nDo not reason from source spelling alone. In an expression, integer promotions and the usual arithmetic conversions can change the type used for the actual calculation. This is especially important when mixing signed and unsigned integers or integer and floating-point values.\n\nFor numeric code, state the desired mathematical domain first, then choose types and conversions that preserve it. Test boundary values and values near precision limits. Avoid relying on an assumed size when portability matters; use the standard guarantees or fixed-width types where appropriate."
