                "title": "Deep mental model",
                "content": "For **Include guards**, separate source-language behavior from toolchain behavior. The preprocessor transforms source before compilation; the compiler translates translation units and diagnoses language constraints; the linker combines object files and resolves external references; the runtime environment then starts and executes the resulting program.\n\nWhen debugging, identify which layer failed. A missing declaration may be a compile-time problem, an unresolved symbol may be a link-time problem, and invalid memory access is typically a runtime correctness problem. Treat the first meaningful diagnostic as evidence rather than chasing every downstream error.\n\nReproducible builds also depend on compiler options, warning levels, language standard, optimization, and linked libraries. Record those assumptions in project documentation and enable strong warnings during development."
